# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Prettier owns TypeScript, JavaScript, JSON and YAML. It does not own
# SQL or Markdown, and both exclusions are deliberate.
#
# SQL: prettier has no SQL parser, and the migrations are hand-aligned
# in columns anyway — a formatter would not preserve that even if it
# could read them.
#
# MARKDOWN: the specs are hand-wrapped prose full of em-dashes, and
# prettier's table alignment miscounts those characters — it emits
# separator rows two columns wider than the content rows it is meant to
# line up with. It also rewrites `*emphasis*` to `_emphasis_` and pads
# every table cell to the width of the longest one, which turns a
# one-word edit into a whole-table diff. Docs are read by people and by
# agents, not rendered from a pipeline, so hand formatting wins here.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

**/dist/**
**/build/**
**/coverage/**
**/node_modules/**
pnpm-lock.yaml
*.sql
